                    Beta(α,α) distribution (with α=0.4) for                     
                    each batch, linearly combining both                         
                    inputs and labels. This regularizes the                     
                    model, improves generalization and can                      
                    reduce overfitting on specific                              
                    skin‐tone groups. Everything else                           
                    remains the same—fine‐tuning                                
                    ResNeXt50_32x4d with 5‐fold stratified                      
                    CV, computing overall AUROC and                             
                    subgroup gaps, retraining on full data,                     
                    and saving the final model. Below is                        
                    the updated implementation.                                 
                    Results: The training and evaluation                        
                    script ran successfully without errors.                     
                    The model achieved a strong mean AUROC                      
                    of 0.9185, indicating good overall                          
                    classification performance. The mean                        
                    AUROC gap between light and dark skin                       
                    tone subgroups was only 0.0125,                             
                    demonstrating fairness towards skin                         
                    tone without compromising accuracy.                         
                    Training completed efficiently within                       
                    the time limit.                                             
                    Validation Metric: 0.9185                                   
                                                                                
