                    Design: I propose fine-tuning a                             
                    pretrained ResNeXt50_32x4d backbone for                     
                    binary malignant vs non-malignant                           
                    classification by replacing its final                       
                    layer. We'll perform 5-fold stratified                      
                    cross-validation to estimate the                            
                    model’s generalization performance and                      
                    compute the AUROC and subgroup AUROC                        
                    gap between dark (skin_tone≤3) and                          
                    light (skin_tone≥5) skin tones to                           
                    monitor fairness. After                                     
                    cross-validation, we'll retrain on the                      
                    full dataset and save the final model.                      
                    A `predict()` function will load the                        
                    saved model and output malignancy                           
                    probabilities for new images.                               
