                    Design: I propose to incorporate simple                     
                    test-time augmentation (TTA) by                             
                    averaging model predictions over the                        
                    original and horizontally flipped                           
                    versions of each validation image,                          
                    which can reduce prediction variance                        
                    and improve AUROC without changing the                      
                    training procedure. During each fold’s                      
                    validation, we will apply both the                          
                    standard resize+normalize transform and                     
                    a horizontal‐flip variant, average                          
                    their sigmoid outputs, and then compute                     
                    overall and subgroup AUROCs on these                        
                    averaged probabilities. The same TTA                        
                    logic will also be integrated into the                      
                    `predict()` function for inference on                       
                    new images.                                                 
