                    Design: We fine-tune a pretrained                           
                    ResNet18 for binary malignant vs                            
                    non-malignant classification, using                         
                    simple augmentations. We perform 5-fold                     
                    stratified cross-validation, computing                      
                    overall AUROC and AUC gap between dark                      
                    (skin_tone≤3) and light (skin_tone≥5)                       
                    subgroups in each fold. The final model                     
                    is saved, and a `predict()` function                        
                    loads it to infer malignancy                                
                    probabilities on new images.                                
                    Results: The training and evaluation                        
                    code ran successfully without any                           
